      en: "The National Museum of Indonesia (Museum Nasional) in Jakarta, also known as Gedung Gajah (Elephant Building), is the largest and oldest museum in the country. It was founded in 1868 by the Dutch colonial government. The museum houses a vast collection of artifacts from across Indonesia, including prehistoric finds, Hindu-Buddhist art, ceramics, textiles, and ethnographic objects. The famous bronze elephant statue in front is a gift from the King of Siam. The museum provides a comprehensive overview of Indonesian history and culture from the Stone Age to modern times.",
