      en: "Keraton Sambas is the royal palace of the Sultanate of Sambas in West Kalimantan. Built in the 19th century, it served as the residence of the sultans. The architecture shows Malay influences with European elements. The complex includes audience halls, living quarters, and a mosque. Today, the palace houses a museum documenting the history of the Sultanate of Sambas, including relations with the Dutch and local culture. Keraton Sambas is an important cultural center for the Malay community in Kalimantan.",
